      "title": "Exact centered squared-defect coercivity and bounded inverse",
      "source": {
        "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A2",
        "edition": "arXiv:2609.06905v1; Lean4.33.0/fixedMathlib",
        "anchor": "PBPS2609.06905v1 AppendixB B1-B5, D1-D2 real L2 stationarity/centering, C4/B15 squared-defect precursor; exact31regions/54items source inventory independently covered.",
        "wording_status": "faithful paraphrase",
        "attribution": "Attributed ASTIS background completion/consumer of Fan Chen, Sinho Chewi, Jianfeng Lu and Matthew S. Zhang Appendix B/D. This is a scoped squared-defect result; it is not the printed Γ theorem or a main mixing theorem."
      },
      "statement": "E is a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume; rank zero is an explicit extension of the source Euclidean convention. V:E→ℝ is C²; 0<α≤β; α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v; η>0 and βη≤1. μ=volume.tilted(−V), J=Law(X,X+√ηZ) for independent X∼μ and Z∼N(0,I), and ν=J.snd. Finite dimensionality of E does not imply finite dimensionality of L²(ν). There exist a selfadjoint bounded operator T on L²(ν) with the literal ν-a.e. action Tu(y)=∫u(x)S(y,dx), where S(y)=volume.tilted(x↦−V((y+x)/2)−‖y−x‖²/(8η)); a class q=1 ν-a.e. with ⟨q,u⟩=∫u dν for all u; and the actual selfadjoint restriction T₀ to H₀=ker⟨q,·⟩. Set ρ=(1−αη)/(1+αη) and δ=4αη/(1+αη)². The squared defect D₀=I_H₀−T₀² is positive. For every u∈H₀, T₀u=Tu as an ambient class, ‖T₀u‖≤ρ‖u‖, ⟨D₀u,u⟩=‖u‖²−‖T₀u‖² and δ‖u‖²≤⟨D₀u,u⟩. D₀ is a unit in the algebra of bounded continuous linear endomorphisms of H₀; hence it has a bounded inverse on this exact centered space. The original hypotheses force δ>0 and include αη=1. No full-space inverse or positive square root is claimed.",
      "assumptions": [
        "The complete potential, curvature, initialization law and step conditions are stated above. No operator, probability, stationarity, mean-zero preservation or coercivity certificate is supplied by the caller.",
        "L² consists of AE classes; finite dimension of E does not make L² finite dimensional. The whole closed mean-zero subspace is used.",
        "Zero-dimensional E is explicitly included as an extension of the source Euclidean convention; αη=1 is retained."
      ],
      "formulae": [
        {
          "label": "Exact centered squared-defect coercivity and bounded inverse",
          "tex": "\\rho=\\frac{1-\\alpha\\eta}{1+\\alpha\\eta},\\quad\\delta=\\frac{4\\alpha\\eta}{(1+\\alpha\\eta)^2}>0,\\quad\\|T_0u\\|\\le\\rho\\|u\\|,\\quad\\langle D_0u,u\\rangle\\ge\\delta\\|u\\|^2,\\quad D_0\\in\\operatorname{GL}(H_0)."
        }
      ],
